CITY CONTRACT#58O1
GENERAL CONTRACT BETWEEN
By:β
Associated Legal Group, LLC, and the City of Cheyenne
Date:.2-15-(2
1.
Parties.The parties to this Contract are Associated Legal Group, LLC,(Contractor),
whose address is 1807Capitol Ave., Suite 203 Cheyenne, WY82001 and the City of
Cheyenne,(City) whose address is 2101 O'Neil Ave., Cheyenne, Wyoming,82001.
2.
Purpose of Contract.The purpose of this contract is to secure the legal services of the
Contractor as needed for the acquisition of property for the East Pershing Boulevard
Reconstruction Project(Phase 4).
3.
Term of Contract and Required Approvals.This Contract is effective when all parties
have executed it and all required approvals have been granted.Theterm of the Contract
is from January 6,2012 to completion of legal services for the project or until one of the
parties terminates thecontract.
4.
Payment.The City agrees to pay the Contractor for the services described herein at a rate
of$220per hour.Payment shall be mademonthly upon submission of monthly invoices.
Except as otherwise provided in this Contract, the City shall pay ordinary costs and
expenses incurred by Contractor in connection with its performance of legal services
under this Contract, provided however, that the Contractor shall provide advance written
notice tothe City of any and all contracts entered into by Contractor with third parties for
the provision of expert witness services, engineering services, surveying services,
appraisal services, and other litigation support services.No third party fees, costs, or
expenses shall be incurred by Contractor without the express prior written approvalof the
City.
5.
Responsibilities of Contractor.The services to be provided by Contractors hall include
legal services associated with and in support of the acquisition of propertyfor City.These
services shall include but are not limited to, counsel and advice, preparation of legal
documents and correspondence, preparation and appearance in court proceedings.
6.
General Provisions
A.
Amendments.Any changes, modifications, revisions, or amendments to this
Contract which aremutually agreedupon by theparties to this Contract shall be
incorporated by written instrument, executed and signedby allparties tothis
Contract.
B.
Applicable Law/Venue.The construction, interpretation, and enforcement of
this Contract shall be governedby the laws of the State of Wyoming.The Courts
of the State of Wyoming shall have jurisdiction over this Contractand theparties,
and thevenue shall be the First Judicial District, Laramie County, Wyoming.The
parties intend and agree that the City does not waive sovereign immunity by
entering into this Contract and specifically retains immunity and all defenses
available to it as a sovereign pursuant to applicable law.
```

